Management of debian/copyright:
===============================
We use cme to manage/update the machine-readable copyright file.


Basic mode for updating to a new upstream version:

* apt install cme libconfig-model-dpkg-perl

* Doublecheck whether manual overrides in debian/fill.copyright.blanks.yml
  are still needed/up to date.

* Doublecheck whether wrangling in debian/fix.scanned.copyright
  is still needed/up to date.

* cp debian/copyright-template debian/copyright
* cme update dpkg-copyright

Now doublecheck the generated copyright file. Add new License:-stanzas to
debian/copyright-template for newly used licenses ("Please fill license
UNKNOWN from header of"), update overrides and/or the list of
ignored/scanned files (debian/copyright-scan-patterns.yml) if necessary.
Rinse and repeat.

https://github.com/dod38fr/config-model/wiki/Updating-debian-copyright-file-with-cme
https://ddumont.wordpress.com/2015/04/05/improving-creation-of-debian-copyright-file/
https://ddumont.wordpress.com/2015/05/31/improving-update-of-existing-debiancopyright-file/
